  "batch_reasoning": "The cluster centers on delivery-process capability rather than one specific coding stack: the examples repeatedly mention DevOps, CI/CD pipelines, and full SDLC coverage from requirements through deployment and maintenance. A second sub-theme is methodology selection and orchestration across modern development frameworks, where React/Vue/FastAPI/Express or Angular/NodeJS appear as implementation contexts rather than the core skill itself. The evidence is coherent enough for a small set of related competencies, but not one single competency, because SDLC management, DevOps automation, and modern-framework application development require different demonstrations of mastery. I would keep DevOps, CI/CD, and SDLC together in one competency about delivery automation and lifecycle management; merge modern frameworks with SDLC only where the framework use is part of building and shipping software; and drop no item, though the duplicate SDLC/DevOps variants are best treated as synonyms within broader competencies. The role spread across DevOps/SRE and software engineering supports a shared capability area focused on modern software delivery practices rather than a narrow job family.",
  "competencies": [
    {
      "title": "Implement DevOps-based CI/CD delivery pipelines",
      "description": "Set up and operate automated build, test, and deployment pipelines that support consistent software delivery. Use DevOps practices to connect version control, pipeline automation, and environment promotion so releases are repeatable and controlled.",
      "related_skills": [
        "DevOps",
        "CI/CD"
      ],
      "rationale": "The evidence repeatedly pairs DevOps with CI/CD pipelines, showing that the intended meaning is automated software delivery rather than general operations work. The examples emphasize building scalable, secure, and automated systems and using pipeline practices as part of development methodology. A learner can demonstrate mastery by configuring a working pipeline that builds, tests, and deploys software with defined release controls. This differs from the other competencies because it focuses on release automation and delivery mechanics, not on the broader lifecycle or the application framework used."
    },
    {
      "title": "Apply full SDLC practices from analysis to deployment",
      "description": "Plan and execute software work across the full development lifecycle, including analysis, design, coding, testing, implementation, deployment, and maintenance. Coordinate work so each phase produces the inputs needed for the next phase and the solution moves cleanly into production.",
      "related_skills": [
        "software development lifecycle (SDLC)",
        "SDLC",
        "DevOps"
      ],
      "rationale": "The source sentences define SDLC as an end-to-end sequence from business requirements through design, implementation, and production deployment, so the competency must cover the whole delivery flow. DevOps is included because in context it reinforces lifecycle coordination and production readiness, not just tooling. Mastery can be shown by producing a complete solution plan and delivering a working feature through testing and deployment with clear phase handoffs. This competency is distinct from CI/CD because it is about governing the full lifecycle, not only automating release steps."
    },
    {
      "title": "Build and deliver applications with modern frameworks",
      "description": "Develop application features using contemporary frameworks and runtime stacks, selecting the framework that fits the problem and integrating it into the broader solution. Use the framework to implement maintainable components that can move through testing and deployment as part of the delivery process.",
      "related_skills": [
        "modern frameworks",
        "software development lifecycle (SDLC)",
        "SDLC"
